From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0339-nemyu-02-held-writes-before-each-list.patch

Source: 0339-nemyu-02-held-writes-before-each-list.patch
Moved by hand: the held writes go through upstream's batched OnCacheInvalidations; declarations placed beside upstream's ForEachPendingCpuWrite

gpu: EDEN_NX2_HELD_WRITES=1 applies held-back CPU writes before each command list

Port of part of Nemyu 3d49423c (Uesleizito Zin, gitlab.com/nemyu-emulator/nemyu, branch nemyu, tag
nemyu-v0.1.4), itself from PokeDinner c3be47da94 (Franseven, git.eden-emu.dev/Franseven/
PokeDinner-a-Eglantine-Fork), from Eden-NS2 15b48a6615. GPL-3.0-or-later, as the core.

A guest CPU write to a page the GPU has written waits in the dirty-memory managers until the GPU
thread applies it. Here that is at fences and a few other points, none tied to a list. The guest
makes the write before it submits the list that may read it, so that list could run on the older
bytes. 0083 says Ocarina writes onto such pages about 230 times a second, and mapped bindings make
more pages GPU-written, so more writes wait.

Changed from the source: off unless EDEN_NX2_HELD_WRITES=1; Nemyu has it on. OnCachedWrite is left
out: 0083 already sends the CPU's bytes into the buffer from WriteMemory, so the fence's
OnCacheInvalidation does what OnCachedWrite was added for. A log line counts the writes this path
applies, because that count is the test: if it stays near 0 the fault is not ours.

Nemyu: 21.1 ms with it, 23.2 without, one run each, its author calls that noise. Expect no speed
from this. It is a correctness change. Whether it changes any picture is a guess.

On the split the apply runs on the back, in the ring ahead of the list, as every other cache call
does. No new gathering thread: Gather stays on the GPU thread or the back, so the race fixed by
Lichii #138 (7e1d645557) does not arise.

Limit, as in the source: this runs where a list is submitted. A list parked on a semaphore acquire
resumes through Scheduler::ResumePending without it, so writes the guest made while the list waited
still land at the next fence. Unset, the split queues nothing (GPU::HeldWritesOn, added for next18).

Core patch. Nothing here has run on a console.

diff --git a/src/video_core/gpu.cpp b/src/video_core/gpu.cpp
index abe02457b7..f6863aaa7d 100644
--- a/src/video_core/gpu.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/gpu.cpp
@@ -69,6 +69,17 @@ u64 Nx2GpuTimeDivisor() {
     }();
     return divisor;
 }
+
+// EDEN_NX2_HELD_WRITES=1: guest CPU writes to GPU-written memory wait in the dirty-memory managers
+// until the GPU thread applies them, otherwise only at the next fence. The guest makes them before
+// it submits the list that may read them, so that list could run on the older bytes.
+bool HeldWritesBeforeLists() {
+    static const bool enabled = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_HELD_WRITES");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1';
+    }();
+    return enabled;
+}
 } // Anonymous namespace
 
 struct GPU::Impl {
@@ -140,6 +151,32 @@ struct GPU::Impl {
         }
     }
 
+    /// Applies held-back guest CPU writes before a submitted list runs. Called by the thread that
+    /// owns the caches: the GPU thread, or the split's back.
+    void ApplyHeldWritesBeforeList() {
+        if (!HeldWritesBeforeLists()) {
+            return;
+        }
+        static u64 count{};
+        static u64 bytes{};
+        static u64 next_log{1};
+        std::vector<std::pair<DAddr, u64>> writes;
+        std::function<void(PAddr, size_t)> callback_writes([&writes](PAddr address, size_t size) {
+            writes.emplace_back(address, size);
+            ++count;
+            bytes += size;
+        });
+        system.GatherGPUDirtyMemory(callback_writes);
+        if (!writes.empty()) {
+            renderer->ReadRasterizer()->OnCacheInvalidations(writes);
+        }
+        if (count >= next_log) {
+            next_log = count * 2;
+            LOG_INFO(HW_GPU, "CPU writes applied before a command list: {} so far, {} KiB", count,
+                     bytes >> 10);
+        }
+    }
+
     void ForEachPendingCpuWrite(const std::function<void(DAddr, size_t)>& callback) {
         for (auto& manager : system.GetGPUDirtyMemoryManager()) {
             manager.ForEachPending(callback);
@@ -492,6 +529,14 @@ void GPU::InvalidateGPUCache() {
     impl->InvalidateGPUCache();
 }
 
+void GPU::ApplyHeldWritesBeforeList() {
+    impl->ApplyHeldWritesBeforeList();
+}
+
+bool GPU::HeldWritesOn() const {
+    return HeldWritesBeforeLists();
+}
+
 void GPU::ForEachPendingCpuWrite(const std::function<void(DAddr, size_t)>& callback) {
     impl->ForEachPendingCpuWrite(callback);
 }
